**Where:**
- $x_i$ is the number of units of product $i$ to fulfill (sell).
- $r_i$ is the revenue per unit for product $i$.
- $\text{Demand}_i$ is the demand for product $i$.
- $\text{Initial Inventory}_i$ is the available inventory for product $i$.

**Summary of constraints:**
- Cannot fulfill more than demand: $x_i \leq \text{Demand}_i$
- Cannot fulfill more than available inventory: $x_i \leq \text{Initial Inventory}_i$
- Cannot fulfill negative quantities: $x_i \geq 0$
- Must fulfill in whole units: $x_i \in \mathbb{Z}_{\geq 0}$

**Complete Model:**
\[
\begin{align*}
\max \quad & \sum_{i} r_i x_i \\
\text{s.t.} \quad & 0 \leq x_i \leq \min\{\text{Demand}_i, \text{Initial Inventory}_i\} \quad \forall i \\
& x_i \in \mathbb{Z}_{\geq 0} \quad \forall i
\end{align*}
\][0m

